    "created_at": "2025-02-07T18:36:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-07T18:36:48Z",
    "body": "> As the title says, it seems like the steps for \"hide popover stack until\" and \"close entire popover list\" expect popoverList to be dynamically updated as items are hidden.\n\nI agree with this - at least in Chromium, those are [implemented](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_element.cc;l=1722;drc=9b045da738d6f6f5218604f66ad5c2c2ca6657a8) as references to a list that is dynamically updated. I'm not sure exactly how a similar concept is built in spec-land, suggestions appreciated.\n\n\n\n> Also, should step 2 in \"hide popover stack until\" iterate popoverList in reverse? It's supposed to find the last item to be hidden, so it seems like it should iterate in the same order as step 4.\n\nYes, for sure. In Chromium the `popoverList` is actually implemented as a stack (same link as above), and the loop repeatedly pops off the stack. Perhaps `popoverList` should just become a stack?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
