    "created_at": "2025-02-11T21:30:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-11T21:30:15Z",
    "body": "> * Mostly revert [Make auto popover list an algorithm #9241](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9241) to make \"showing auto/hint popover list\" a property of the document. (i.e. \"The Document has a showing auto popover list and a showing hint popover list, which are lists of HTML Elements, initially empty.\")\n\n+@annevk for comment, since that was originally how things were written, but Anne preferred not to have more lists.\n\nGenerally, I'd be very happy with that state of things, since it's much closer to the implementation, at least for Chromium.\n\n> Another thing to consider is that the chromium implementation defines the showing auto popover stack differently from the current spec as it also includes some hint popovers.\n\nUgh, this is a good catch. And those are very intentional: if you have a `popover=auto` that contains a `popover=hint`, the hint goes onto the `auto` stack. That's tested in [this WPT](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/popovers/popover-light-dismiss-hint.html), among others. The change to explicit lists will also fix this problem.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
